3601206001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"## Context\nThe generated configuration reference contains an unsupported MCP exposure claim and lacks public descriptions for emitted settings. Hand-authored configuration guidance also contains stale ADR references and diagnostic-switch state. `consensual-ignored-ivorygull` records the accepted generator design. ADR 0086 and ADR 0087 provide current decision references.\n\n## Plan\n- Complete three bounded child tasks for generator narrative, setting descriptions, and current-state guidance.\n- Preserve generator ownership of `docs/config-reference.md`.\n- Keep each child behavior-neutral.\n- Do not create an MCP configuration tool.\n- Do not decide the deferred F05 generated-artifact catalog.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] F19A removes the nonexistent MCP configuration-surface claim through the generator.\n- [x] F19B provides one generated public description for every emitted typed setting.\n- [x] F19C corrects ADR references and diagnostic-switch guidance.\n- [x] Generated files remain source-owned and drift checked.\n- [x] All children pass applicable targeted checks and land independently.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_config_schema.py","reason":"Child F19B adds public setting descriptions while retaining every configuration dataclass under the configuration-read gate."},{"path":"src/rebar/_config_coercion.py","reason":"Child F19B extracts low-level validation helpers along the existing coercion seam."},{"path":"scripts/gen_config_reference.py","reason":"Children F19A and F19B correct generated configuration ownership."},{"path":"docs/config-reference.md","reason":"Children regenerate the external configuration reference."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_gen_config_reference.py","reason":"Children pin generator correctness."},{"path":"docs/config.md","reason":"Child F19C corrects maintained configuration guidance."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyri